* ============================================================================
* workspace_v3_selflocate.dts -- DTSHEMA 3 step 1 (owner-chartered 2026-08-11):
* opt-in v3 payloads carry FLAVOR plus DBFROOT/IDXROOT/LMDBROOT declarative
* lines, and a v3 load resolves its AREA entries against the PAYLOAD's roots,
* not the current environment (self-locating posture). Global SETPATH slots
* are never mutated; LMDBROOT is recorded-not-applied (owner: "lmdb only for
* disks" -- application chartered).
*
* Proof shape: save mcc_x64's posture as v3 into the catalog, then BREAK the
* environment on purpose (SETPATH to the default roots, where no MCC table
* lives) and load it back. Restoration despite the wrong environment IS the
* proof. Coexistence guard: WORKSPACE_MEMO must run green on the same build
* (v3 is opt-in; v2 producers and consumers stay untouched).
*
* Run: DO workspace_v3_selflocate  |  regression: REGRESSION RUN WORKSPACE_V3
* Markers: V3_T1 (STUDENTS row readable through the self-located load).
* RUNTIME-PROVEN 2026-08-11 (build 14:47:06) by hand before promotion: WSID M6,
* FLAVOR X64, both roots echoed, 13 areas restored from the wrong environment.
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

FORMULA "WS-V3-PROOF-BEGIN"

* --- environment-first: the save leg runs from the real x64 roots -----------
*
* AMENDED 2026-08-28. THIS LEG USED TO READ 'WORKSPACE LOAD mcc_x64', AND THAT
* LINE IS WHY THIS SPEC COULD NOT BE BRACKETED. mcc_x64 is a posture FILE in the
* PRODUCTION workspaces directory, so the spec read production to build its own
* fixture -- and once REGRESSION runs it with the WORKSPACES slot redirected at
* a scratch root (AIF-078 L2), that file is not there and the load finds
* nothing. The spec now BUILDS ITS OWN POSTURE, which is what every
* self-bootstrapping spec in this corpus already does.
*
* IT ALSO REMOVES A DEPENDENCY ON A MUTABLE ARTIFACT NOBODY OWNS. mcc_x64
* .dtschema can be re-saved by any session; if it changes, this spec's meaning
* changes with NOTHING going red. That is history-dependence wearing a green
* suit -- the same shape the identity ladder found in the thirteen live catalog
* heads, one level up.
*
* THE FIXTURE IS THINNER AND THAT COST IS STATED: mcc_x64 restored THIRTEEN
* areas, this restores TWO. The count was never the claim -- V3_T1 asserts that
* a row is READABLE through a payload whose roots disagree with the live
* environment, and one area proves that mechanism exactly as well as thirteen.
* Two rather than one deliberately, so the posture is not degenerate.
*
* STUDENTS IS OPENED INTO AREA 8 ON PURPOSE: mcc_x64 held it at AREA 8 and the
* assertion below reads SELECT 8. Keeping the slot keeps the marker and its
* meaning untouched, so this amendment changes the FIXTURE and not the PROOF.
* Addressing is by slot and never by name because SELECT <name> is unscoped
* (see relation_parent_workspace_crossing.dts).
SETPATH DBF DBF/X64
SETPATH INDEXES INDEXES/X64
WORKSPACE CLOSE
SELECT 1
USE DEPT
SELECT 8
USE STUDENTS
WORKSPACE SAVE v3_regress MEMO V3
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- break the environment on purpose ---------------------------------------
SETPATH DBF DBF
SETPATH INDEXES INDEXES

* --- self-location: the payload's roots must find the tables ----------------
WORKSPACE LOAD v3_regress MEMO
* CORRECTED 2026-08-28, SAME DAY, AFTER A FALSE GREEN. This assertion used to
* address the table by SLOT (SELECT 8), and the amendment above kept slot 8 on
* the reasoning that the old fixture held STUDENTS there. THAT REASONING WAS
* VOID: R130 says a posture's AREA numbers are KEYS, NOT ADDRESSES, and the
* load prints so -- tables land at slots 0..N-1. The old fixture only worked
* because mcc_x64 restored THIRTEEN areas, so slot 8 coincidentally held
* STUDENTS. With a small posture SELECT 8 reaches NOTHING -- and the marker
* still printed .T., because a marker over a closed area does not error, it
* picks a side (see claude/FINDING_MARKER_OVER_A_CLOSED_AREA_PICKS_A_SIDE.md).
* ADDRESSING BY NAME SURVIVES RELOCATION, which is why workspace_memo and
* workspace_load_shortfall stayed sound through the same change.
SELECT STUDENTS
TOP
? "V3_T1_selflocated_students_row:" + (SID >= 1)

FORMULA "WS-V3-PROOF-END"

* --- teardown: close and restore the x64 disk environment -------------------
WORKSPACE CLOSE
SETPATH DBF DBF/X64
SETPATH INDEXES INDEXES/X64
